\p{The 200 wrong rejections by cause: F1 146, F2 30, F3 10, F4 1, F5 13. Every one is accepted by the base build, by the mode \code{deferred} and by the reference engine. No export is declined by the candidate or ends in an error; the machine declines no unit of any generated export.}

\p{\strong{The other engines on the same 3,683 exports.} The reference engine of the candidate gives the official verdict on every one. The mode \code{deferred} gives the base build's verdict on every one: no rejection of an official accept, 1,385 accepts of official rejections, none of them of a false-step export. The mode \code{shared} differs from \code{local} on 301 exports: it rejects 190 official accepts (the 200 of \code{local} without the 10 of F3) and accepts 849 official rejections, 291 of them rejections that \code{local} gets right. All 284 false-step exports are rejected by every engine, every mode and every schedule variant.}
}

\subtree{
